    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_title:ca0a4d6daf445776",
      "field": "itinerary.title",
      "sourceTextSha256": "79eba2616ca6f2e3fda91754374ab5abd53f65f93b663a5977c8b6810c009209",
      "text": "Quito: TelefériQo and Rucu Pichincha",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw96l01v-myqa6co0d78doi5ozugapb",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      }
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "ad66c545c9d8101bab1b6d6b036232ae4c034cc5fa3b8eb422939083b75ff6ca",
      "text": "After breakfast, set out for a day of sightseeing lasting about 8 hours, including transfers.\n\nIn the morning, head to the TelefériQo cable car. It starts at 2,950 m and takes about 20 minutes to reach the viewpoint at 4,053 m. The line is about 2.5 km long. From the top, you can see Quito and the mountains surrounding the capital.\n\nContinue to the top of Cruz Loma hill. From there, hike for about 2 hours towards the base of Rucu Pichincha, an extinct volcano that rises to 4,794 m. The trail looks out over Quito and the surrounding volcanoes. On a clear day, you can see Cotopaxi, Antisana, Cayambe and other peaks.\n\nA packed lunch is provided. Return to your hotel in the afternoon.\n\n**Accommodation:** Mercure 4-star.  \n**Meals:** breakfast and packed lunch.",
      "provenance": {
